      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What standards support data handling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS can discuss NIST SP 800-88 methods, HIPAA-related safeguards, ISO 27001 controls, and customer-specific procedures during project planning. The selected method depends on media type, risk profile, contractual requirements, and requested documentation. Under HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312, organizations must apply appropriate safeguards to electronic protected health information."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS supports Bakersfield, Shafter, Arvin, Oildale, and surrounding Kern County service needs. Pickup planning can cover offices, schools, clinics, farms, warehouses, plants, and government buildings when volume and access requirements are reviewed. Organizations searching for electronic recycling near me throughout Bakersfield can request scheduled pickup across Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup may be available at no cost for qualifying volumes and accepted equipment. Contact STS with the approximate inventory, location, access details, and preferred timing so the team can review the project. The secure fleet serves Bakersfield with scheduled pickups throughout Kern County and near major regional freight routes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Documentation depends on the services selected and may include pickup records, asset details, chain-of-custody information, data handling records, and downstream reporting. Request documentation requirements before scheduling. Most IT managers expect records that connect equipment identification, collection activity, and final disposition, especially during refreshes involving multiple buildings."
          }
        }
      ]
